{"items":[{"id":"49OaEWzyRHknuncYVuk1ID","slug":"the-best-enterprise-sales-dialers-compliance-admin-controls-and-scale","title":"The best enterprise sales dialers in 2026","metaTitle":"The best enterprise sales dialers in 2026","publishedDate":"2026-09-20","seoDescription":"The best enterprise sales dialers ranked on compliance, admin controls, and scale, with per-seat economics and TCPA guardrails compared.","readTime":"9 minutes","tag":"Sales Tools","keyTakeAways":{"metadata":{"tags":[],"concepts":[]},"sys":{"space":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"Space","id":"kyprwggh4muz"}},"id":"1cMwG5OtOS49RYRPxLTvSX","type":"Entry","createdAt":"2026-09-20T02:01:41.255Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-20T02:01:41.255Z","environment":{"sys":{"id":"master","type":"Link","linkType":"Environment"}},"publishedVersion":1,"revision":1,"contentType":{"sys":{"type":"Link","linkType":"ContentType","id":"blogKeyTakeaways"}},"locale":"en-US"},"fields":{"keyTakeAways":[{"keyTakeAways":"Artisan bundles a compliant dialer inside a full AI sales platform, priced through usage-based credits rather than a premium per-seat dialer license, whereas dedicated parallel dialers typically charge $200-300+ per user per month."},{"keyTakeAways":"Per-lead compliance is the enterprise differentiator: lead-local calling-hours enforcement and do-not-call suppression that apply automatically before a call connects, not as a manual checkbox."},{"keyTakeAways":"Nooks and Orum lead on line count for high-volume call floors; most enterprise teams do not need that ceiling."},{"keyTakeAways":"Per-number reputation visibility, daily call ceilings, and number warm-up protect connect rates across a large team, that is the failure mode that kills enterprise calling programs without anyone noticing."},{"keyTakeAways":"Central admin with CRM owner mapping means calls log to the right rep automatically and callbacks route to the right phone, which matters far more at 100 seats than at 5."},{"keyTakeAways":"Pooled org-level numbers, billed separately from seats, replace the per-seat number sprawl that legacy dialers bill for."}],"blogName":"The best enterprise sales dialers in 2026"}},"heroImage":{"url":"https://images.ctfassets.net/kyprwggh4muz/PszRRpX7tRBD6jXAw0QM4/c5f11b3f1061c8f5d73917893d605691/enterprise-sales-dialers-cover.webp","width":2389,"height":1120,"title":"The best enterprise sales dialers in 2026"},"content":{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"For most enterprise sales organizations the best dialer is Artisan, because it puts compliant calling inside one AI-run outbound platform, governed centrally rather than bolted on as a standalone tool. Teams whose entire motion is maximum-volume call-floor dialing should still look at dedicated parallel dialers like Nooks or Orum, which specialize in high-volume parallel calling.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"That answer only holds if you evaluate a dialer the way a VP of Sales or a RevOps lead actually has to: not on raw line count, but on whether it enforces compliance per lead, whether admins can govern it centrally, and whether the per-seat cost stays sane when you multiply it across a hundred reps. This guide ranks the field on those terms.","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Comparison table","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"heading-2"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Dialer","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Best for","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"},{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"content":[{"data":{},"marks":[],"value":"Standout capability","nodeType":"text"}],"nodeType":"paragraph"}],"nodeType":"table-header-cell"}